    {
      "Seq": 17,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Plain",
      "Area": "Hedgerow",
      "LocationId": 32010,
      "Actor": "Eghbert Moorshield",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I find myself walking along the hedgerow, in the morning, as I did when I used to play among the thorny bushes, gathering mushrooms to survive. The scene is reminiscent of those days, with a hare, a patch of flowers, a gate bar, a water meadow, and an oak tree standing between two open stretches. I am reminded of playing among the trees, the soft weeping willows always whispering secrets to the earth. Their long fronds trailing gently, much like how I used to sway in the breeze, my imagination lost in tales of the dead.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 3,
      "Block": 0,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 18,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Plain",
      "Area": "Hedgerow",
      "LocationId": 32010,
      "Actor": "Eghbert Moorshield",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I perceive a thorny bush, its drupelets heavy and dark, swelled to their prime. I wish to examine it closely, relying on the simple methods of country folk.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 3,
      "Block": 1,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 19,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Plain",
      "Area": "Hedgerow",
      "LocationId": 32010,
      "Actor": "Eghbert Moorshield",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I want not to stand and look, but to work, to handle the soil and the beasts, to plow and plant. The berry bush stands still, its berries tempting, but I know my hands and the task calls me forth.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 3,
      "Block": 3,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 20,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Plain",
      "Area": "Hedgerow",
      "LocationId": 32010,
      "Actor": "Eghbert Moorshield",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I will not linger, for the berry\u0027s time is ripe, and my hand knows well the hour it should be plucked. I could still examine the berry bush closely, another way. I will rely on the cutting of joints, for it holds the scent and colour of the ripest time, before they spoil on the branch.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 3,
      "Block": 1,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 21,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Plain",
      "Area": "Hedgerow",
      "LocationId": 32010,
      "Actor": "Eghbert Moorshield",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I failed to examine the berry bush closely, a mistake that severed the thread of my thoughts, leaving clean cuts of regret in my mind\u0027s blade.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 3,
      "Block": 3,
      "Key": ""
    },
