    {
      "Seq": 23,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Plain",
      "Area": "Hedgerow",
      "LocationId": 32010,
      "Actor": "Eghbert Moorshield",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I remember playing among the grass, pretending to be dead. This water meadow echoes the soft, verdant fields of my childhood, where I gathered mushrooms. I glance at a flower patch, recalling how I once played among such wildflowers, bees always buzzing between them. I let my focus go, where once I wandered through fields, ignoring the harvest now ripe, just as I did then, when the looters passed and my attention wandered.",
